WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.969
-My next guest is
an Emmy-nominated actress.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.470
Her new series, "Physical,"

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.373
premieres June 18th
on Apple TV Plus.

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:09.776
Here is Rose Byrne!

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.244
Yeah!

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.513
Oh, I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:14.513 --> 00:00:15.782
-Hey, man!

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:18.050
Oh, my God!
You're back in the studio!

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.318
-I'm in the studio. I'm back.

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:21.220
We have an audience.
We have a full audience.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.988
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.988 --> 00:00:24.924
It is -- Thank you, buddy.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.092
You know, you did our show

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.927
when we were doing our show
from my home,

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.029
and I really appreciate you
doing that, you and Bobby.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:31.464
That was really awesome.
I appreciate that.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.498
You're the best.

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:34.033
-So good to see you back there.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:37.336
-You're in Australia.
Is that correct?

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:40.005
-I think so, yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:41.474
-Yeah.
-It's early.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.510
I got up really early, so --

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.046
But you guys are --
It's like late night there.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.481
It's a big -- You're having fun.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.715
-Yeah. This is New York
at nighttime,

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:52.017
and that's Australia at daytime
is where you are.

00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:54.921
-Wait, I'm in the future.
I'm in the future.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.256
-You were born and raised
there in Australia.

00:00:57.256 --> 00:01:01.160
How does Bobby take
going to Australia?

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.996
He's New York.
New Jersey? Where is he --

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.998
-Yeah, he's from Jersey

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:09.401
via, you know, Florida,
Puerto Rico, you know, but he --

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:11.771
He's great, you know?
He's such a champ.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.972
He loves Australia.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.608
It's a beautiful country
and a great city.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:18.111
He just --
He can't get down with Vegemite,

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:21.313
so that's been, like,
a bit of a issue.

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:23.650
-Yeah, Vegemite is a thing,
yeah. I mean, I --

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.384
I've never had it.

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:26.986
Hugh Jackman actually came on

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.387
and made it
the right way for me,

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:31.390
because I've tried it on dares,
and I just do it wrong.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.227
What is the -- What's the key?
'Cause it does --

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.930
Sometimes it just tastes
like, well, poison maybe.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.197
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.066
Something like that.
-Yeah, or like axle grease

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.300
a little bit?
-Yes, grease.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.436
Yes, it tastes like a grease,
a salty grease.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:47.173
-The key is butter. Butter.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:50.009
-Ah. Wait, butter first.
Then Vegemite.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:54.046
-Yeah, just a lot of butter
and very little --

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:56.382
I don't know how Hugh
made it for you.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.884
-Very little.
-But for me, that is --

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.619
Yeah, very little
of the actual Vegemite

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:02.588
and just a lot of butter.

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:05.491
-Can I -- Is it good for you?

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.526
It sounds like
it should be good for you.

00:02:07.526 --> 00:02:10.363
-It's, uh --
It's not, not good for you.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.632
-[ Laughs ] That's their slogan?

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.934
"It's not, not good for you."
-Exactly.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.436
-I want to ask you a question.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:22.442
I saw this beautiful photo of
your living room, of your home.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.543
And --

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.445
-Aww. I haven't been there
for so long.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.013
-Yeah.
-Oh, my gosh, there it is.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.182
-Now, here -- Can we just
zoom in for a second?

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:32.051
Is that a cardboard cutout
of Rod Stewart?

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.120
-Yeah. How fabulous is he?

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.255
Look at that.
-No, he's the coolest. But --

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:37.723
Is that real? What's happening?

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.792
Why is Rod Stewart
in your house?

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.427
Are you a big Rod Stewart fan?

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.528
-Yeah.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:43.730
Not -- I mean --

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.164
Well, he --

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:47.199
It's quite --

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:49.335
So, what happened was --

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.871
-"So what had happened was --"

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.506
-He's -- Look, he's
part of the family now.

00:02:54.506 --> 00:02:57.177
The kids refer to him
as like Uncle Rod,

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:59.245
Roddy Rod Stewart.
He's always there.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.679
-He's Rod the mod, man.
He's cool.

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:03.182
But why is he
in your living room?

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:05.652
-Well, so,
Bobby did this show, "Vinyl"

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.787
where he played
a record executive.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:11.591
And so he had this,
you know, fancy office

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.826
with, you know,
all the rock stars.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:17.830
And, you know, so he had this
massive cutout of Rod Stewart.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.132
And we brought it back
kind of as a joke,

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:22.802
and then it's become
part of the family,

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.269
part of the home.

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:25.638
-I want to talk about

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.840
some of your projects,
if you don't mind.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.243
"Peter Rabbit 2"
is out this weekend.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.245
That's going to be big
for the kids.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.246
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.315
-Yeah. Really fun.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:38.317
-It's fantastic.
And then kind of the opposite,

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:41.454
that I would say is probably
not for kids is "Physical,"

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.588
which I love.

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:43.655
It's set in the '80s.

00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:45.157
You're very '80s in this.

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:47.026
It is well done,
whoever did the sets,

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.562
and the wardrobe,
by the way, is fantastic.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.265
Can you set up what the show
is about for everyone?

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:54.600
-Yeah. I play Sheila Rubin.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.803
She's kind of a very --
We meet her at a breaking point.

00:03:57.803 --> 00:03:59.071
She's in
a dysfunctional marriage

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:01.674
and harboring, like,
a dark secret.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:04.210
And she discovers aerobics

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.812
and kind of finds a way
out of her situation

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:09.549
and becomes kind of empowered,

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:13.419
uses her like, you know --
her illness for good.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:16.656
And, yeah, it's set right at
that turning point of the '80s

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.124
where it's still
kind of the '70s,

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:21.293
and then, like, the world of,
like, home video is coming up

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:22.762
and the mall,

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:25.231
and, like, Ronald Reagan's
just been elected president.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.367
So it sort of straddles
two worlds,

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.101
very much like Sheila,
like, in her head

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:31.771
and then how she appears.
So, it's a lot of fun

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.240
and very --
a really complicated character.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.808
And yeah, I'm excited
for people to see it.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:36.976
-It's on Apple TV Plus,

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.844
and you're fantastic
in everything you do.

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:40.146
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.848
Here's Rose Byrne in "Physical."

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.181
Take a look.

00:04:43.181 --> 00:04:44.784
-[ Laughs ] Are you okay?

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:45.951
-Hi! Oh, yes.

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:47.320
[ Chuckling ] I'm sorry --

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.822
I-I just didn't get enough --
-Breakfast.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.790
-Sleep.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:54.627
-No. Anyway,
so, when Ernie told me

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:58.097
that Danny was asking about
support, I was so excited.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.965
Um --
-Who's Ernie?

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:02.701
-My husband.
-Oh, yes.

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.303
-He's chairman
of the San Diego Civics Club,

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:05.437
and they pretty much decide

00:05:05.437 --> 00:05:07.206
who is and isn't getting
campaign support.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:09.475
I thought I told you this.
No, I know I did, yeah.

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:11.110
-Yes. Yes, yes, yes --
No, of course.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.645
-Yeah, but, yeah,
you weren't listening to me,

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.413
'cause I'm a boring,
fat housewife who's like --

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:16.915
-No. No, no, don't say that.
You look great.

00:05:16.915 --> 00:05:18.518
-Oh, thank you.
It's a new dress.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:20.853
-[ Thinking ] That's exactly
who she is. Fat, boring.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.454
Who would listen to her?
Who would want to --

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:24.724
Her. That's where you're headed.
That's where you'll end up.

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:27.660
I'm so sorry, I have to go.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.695
-I mean, that's --

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:31.196
Come on.

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:32.331
Rose Byrne, everybody.

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:35.567
"Physical" will be streaming
on Apple TV Plus

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:37.236
beginning June 18th.

